# PREDICTION for ROOT lane run 17, committed ALONE and BEFORE the run.
#
# STEP -1 of `scratch/lane-run-7-procedure.md`. The derivation is written out so it is
# checkable independently of whether the number matches. Not decorative: R19-06, R20-07 and
# D0A-R26-06 are three runs whose FIGURE was right and whose EXPLANATION was wrong — the last
# of them in this file. A matching number is not evidence the reasoning was sound.
#
# ORDERING IS CONVENTION, NOT MECHANISM (D0A-R22-01, reopened). Held for runs 13-16.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY RUN 17 IS OWED
#
# Run 16 was clean, and it was the first run whose membership was proven by identity. But it
# ran at `09dc36b`, BEFORE the round-28 remediation, and none of this has executed at root:
#   * `read_frame` / `read_frame_untrusted` SPLIT (D0A-R28-01) — the deadline moved out of the
#     shared reader, where it had capped human consent at 30 s, to the daemon's call site.
#   * the BOUNDED DAEMON EXIT (D0A-R28-02) — `reap_within` + grace + SIGKILL, replacing an
#     unconditional `waitpid` on the untrusted AI. **This one is root-relevant in a way the
#     others are not: it is in `delphi-runtimed`, whose only root exercise is
#     `b1_daemon_binary_runs_the_assembled_flow` — which SKIPS on this lane.**
#   * the acceptance-time deadline check (D0A-R28-03).
#   * the program-fd seal regression tests (D0A-R28-06).
#   * three digest-binding tests (env names, pending_id, timeout).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DERIVATION
#
# Base: run 16 measured EXECUTED 200 / SKIPPED 5 / reported 205 at root, membership proven by
#       identity (205 pairs each side, zero in either direction).
#       Current unprivileged pair: EXECUTED 188 / SKIPPED 25 / reported 213 (measured
#       2026-09-07 at 0cd1a34, re-measured by the pre-commit hook across all 17 targets).
#
# Delta since run 16: the round-28 remediation added EIGHT tests and removed none. Each was
# checked for root-gating BY GREP of its body — geteuid, a SKIP branch, a bwrap_available
# guard, a path-existence branch:
#
#   wire.rs     read_frame_does_not_bound_a_wait_on_a_cooperating_peer       no gate
#   wire.rs     a_frame_whose_last_byte_arrives_after_the_deadline_is_...    no gate
#   execute.rs  an_unsealed_program_fd_is_refused_even_when_its_digest_...   no gate
#   execute.rs  a_partially_sealed_program_fd_is_refused                     no gate
#   execute.rs  a_fully_sealed_program_fd_passes_the_seal_check              no gate
#   action.rs   the_digest_binds_environment_variable_names_not_only_...     no gate
#   action.rs   the_digest_binds_the_pending_id_so_a_token_cannot_cross_...  no gate
#   action.rs   the_digest_binds_the_timeout_even_though_nothing_enforces... no gate
#
# So:  200 + 8 = 208 EXECUTED, skip set unchanged at 5, reported 213.
#
# THREE OF THE EIGHT CALL `execute_approved`, so their ROOT behaviour differs from their
# unprivileged behaviour — and the derivation has to say why the counts still hold:
#   * the two REFUSAL tests assert `Err(UnsealedScript)`, and the seal check runs BEFORE any
#     spawn or credential drop. Root cannot reach a different verdict.
#   * `a_fully_sealed_program_fd_passes_the_seal_check` asserts only that the failure is NOT
#     the seal error. At root the action proceeds further (real credential drop, real bwrap)
#     and may end Ok or Err for sandbox reasons — **both satisfy a negative assertion**, which
#     is exactly why it was written negatively.
#
# CONSISTENCY CHECK: unprivileged 188 + 25 = 213; root 208 + 5 = 213.
# **AND THE EQUALITY IS NOT THE EVIDENCE (D0A-R27-04).** §4b compares `(target, test-name)`
# identities as counters. Run 16 established that check on a tree where nothing had changed;
# **run 17 is the first where it could actually detect something**, because eight tests were
# added between the runs. Expect 213 identities each side and zero in either direction — and if
# a delta appears, it must be nameable as exactly these eight, by name, not by count.
#
# Root and unprivileged remain OVERLAPPING SETS: three of the five root skips execute
# unprivileged. 208 > 188 is NOT a coverage claim.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TIMING TOLERANCES — named in advance so a failure is DIAGNOSED, not re-run
#
# TWO of the eight are timing-dependent, both in `wire.rs`:
#   read_frame_does_not_bound_...     a 900 ms writer delay; asserts the read SUCCEEDS
#   a_frame_whose_last_byte_...       80 ms deadline, final byte at ~150 ms; asserts REFUSAL
#
# **These two fail in OPPOSITE directions under load, which is what makes them a pair.** A slow
# machine cannot make both pass by accident: the first needs a wait NOT to be cut short, the
# second needs a deadline to fire. If only one fails, read which — it says whether the deadline
# is too eager or not eager enough. If BOTH fail, suspect the harness (Iron Law #15 clause 5),
# and DEMONSTRATE that rather than assuming it.
#
# Carrying from run 16's list: `boot_secs_agrees_…` (1 s sampling gap) and the two round-27
# deadline tests (400 ms absolute, `elapsed < 5 s`).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE MUTATION CAMPAIGN IS AN UNPRIVILEGED RESULT, AND THIS RUN DOES NOT CHANGE THAT
#
# `scripts/mutation-campaign.py` produced 14/14 valid experiments at `3593fa8` with
# `euid=1000` recorded. **A green run 17 does not extend those results to root**, and nothing
# in this lane run is a mutation campaign. The harness's own docstring now records what a root
# campaign would require — build unprivileged, run the binaries under sudo, keep artifact
# writes unprivileged, record the TESTS' euid rather than the harness's — so that gap is
# written down rather than waiting to be discovered by someone assuming the unprivileged table
# covers root.
#
# Concretely: the five root-gated tests have never been mutation-tested at all, and one of them
# (`b1_daemon_binary_runs_the_assembled_flow`) is the ONLY exercise of the code R28-02 changed.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT A GREEN RUN 17 WILL NOT ESTABLISH
#
# 1. R28-02's bounded exit is barely exercised. Its code lives in `delphi-runtimed`, whose only
#    root test SKIPS on this lane for want of `--features insecure-test-seams`. A green run 17
#    says almost nothing about it; the unprivileged suite says nothing at all.
# 2. THE SUSPEND DIVERGENCE. Unmeasured; the clock test prints its own delta and states it
#    cannot distinguish the clocks here.
# 3. THE PENDING STORE HAS NO CAP, and the ABANDONED READ WORKER is unbounded for repeated
#    service — 30 s is an engineering choice, not a demonstrated bound.
# 4. `action.timeout` IS ENFORCED NOWHERE (R9-04). Round 28 closed its digest BINDING only, and
#    the test name says so.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A MISMATCH IS A RESULT. Record which side was wrong. Do not adjust this derivation until it
# agrees with the measurement.

EXPECTED_EXECUTED=208
EXPECTED_SKIPPED=5
EXPECTED_REPORTED=213
